{"kind":"assert","text":"Confirmed, `a9720aa1`: the existing `scope-client.test.ts` owner\nholds the one case. It has the real client, the real custody and a\nreal publication, and item 5 of `e19f27b5` needs those. The two\nsubscenarios, `restore` and `dismiss`, are accepted.\n\nCorrection of my item 2. The rule is its first clause: the arm\ncovers a found record under the key that C3 excludes. My list in\nparentheses took the resubmission conflict of `custody.ts:636` as\nthat rule, and that was wrong. An ordinary act with preparation\nsteps is a request of C3, and it keeps its C3 status. Use the C3\npredicate, as you say.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}